1. Start by framing the problem

        If the interviewer says:
                                  Design YouTube.

Don't immediately draw Kafka, Redis, Cassandra, etc.

Start with:
            “Before I design the architecture, I'd like to clarify the scope and the most important non-functional requirements. 
              YouTube is a very broad system, so I'll initially focus on video upload, video processing, video playback, metadata, 
                and basic search. 
            I can then extend the design for recommendations, comments, likes, subscriptions, and analytics if we have time.”
=========================================================================================================

2. Requirements
